# Language statistics should describe what is written here.
#
# Two trees are not. `.yidam/.vendor/` is the yidam template layer, tracked so a clone is
# self-contained rather than because it is authored in this repository. `.yidam/sources/` is
# archived primary source material — legislature and encyclopedia pages downloaded and
# committed so the claims resting on them cannot silently change. Between them they hold most
# of the bytes a language breakdown counts, and none of those bytes were written here.
#
# `linguist-vendored` also collapses these paths by default in pull request review. Neither
# tree is edited by hand, so that is usually right — but it does mean an accidental edit under
# `.vendor/` arrives folded shut, and nothing else in the gate looks for one.
.yidam/.vendor/** linguist-vendored=true
.yidam/sources/** linguist-vendored=true

# `.yidam/catalog/` records a sha256 for each committed source and says the corpus's claims
# rest on those exact bytes. Line-ending normalization on checkout would falsify every digest
# without anyone touching the repository.
.yidam/sources/** -text
